  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 252 PM EDT Tue Sep 29 2026\n\n- Rain Wednesday into Friday\n\nAn upper low across the western CONUS will move east and pull \nmoisture from an Eastern Pacific tropical cyclone with it, which \nspreads in a narrow ribbon along a nearly-east west frontal \nboundary by mid-week. We expect the rain to arrive Wednesday\nmorning and continue on and off through Friday as the front moves\nslowly southeast, nearly parallel with the upper flow. Total QPF \nfrom this event is still expected to be 1 to 2 inches by the time\nit ends on Friday, but we will have to watch if it overperforms \nfrom the injection of tropical moisture. \n\n- Cool air follows the rain\n\nUpper troughing follows for the weekend into early next week with\nCanadian surface highs bringing the coolest air of the season so\nfar. Temperatures are expected to fall below normal across the \nforecast area with frost and freezing temperatures widespread \nSaturday morning and again Tuesday morning as another Canadian \nsurface high moves south early next.",
